we tell other people stories about our

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:08.990
lives? Mark W. Travis, Author/Screenwriter/Director: What are the primary reasons we
tell people stories about our lives?

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:15.210
First of all it's varied. A lot of
reasons but the I think the important

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:18.830
thing you have to realize is that you do
it almost every day

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:24.180
you will tell somebody something about
your life what happened to you in the

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:28.560
morning what happened to you yesterday
in other words it's a primary way of

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.570
connecting with people it's just to tell
them what happened in our lives even if

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:37.140
someone says how are you we're the same
finds it I'm fine except the other day

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:40.890
this is what happened and then you have
a little bit of your story so the

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:44.760
reasons getting back to your question
the reason we tell people stories about

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:54.059
our lives are multiple one is to connect
one is to be seen another is to actually

00:00:54.059 --> 00:00:59.910
hide you can tell a story from your life
and hide an aspect of yourself or the

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.899
truth about yourself by telling another
story you can tell a story in your life

00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:09.390
to avoid what the conversation is about
you can tell a story in your life to get

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:15.780
attention to feel important you can tell
a story a part of a story of your life

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:22.830
to actually feel vulnerable and to get
sympathy or empathy so there's a wide

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:28.920
range of reasons we sometimes
intuitively instinctively tell the

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:33.540
stories from our life that tell what's
going on in fact just before this

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:37.860
interview I won't go into them but all
